      "source": [
        "# Exhausted\n",
        "\n",
        "An iterator is exhausted when it has no more values and raises `StopIteration`. Once exhausted, it must continue to do so on subsequent calls to `__next__()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-exhausted)"
      ]
    }
  ],
